meta {
  name: Create user
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/users
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "username": "{{newUsername}}",
    "email": "{{newEmail}}",
    "password": "{{newPassword}}",
    "role": "{{newRole}}"
  }
}

script:post-response {
  if (res.status >= 200 && res.status < 300 && res.body?.id) {
    bru.setVar("userId", res.body.id);
  }
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 201
}

docs {
  # Create user

  `POST /api/users`

  Create an active user and hash the password using BCrypt.

  ## Authentication

  Admin; inherited Bearer token.

  ## Parameters

  No path or query parameters.

  ## Request body

  | Field | Type | Rules / default |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | username, email, password | string | Non-nullable fields; no explicit email format or password length attributes in this DTO. |
  | role | string enum | Admin or Editor; Editor if omitted. |

  Send Content-Type: application/json.

  ```json
  {
    "username": "{{newUsername}}",
    "email": "{{newEmail}}",
    "password": "{{newPassword}}",
    "role": "{{newRole}}"
  }
  ```

  ## Response

  HTTP **201**.

  ```json
  {
    "id": "11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111",
    "username": "Example editor",
    "email": "editor@example.com",
    "role": "Editor",
    "isActive": true,
    "createdAt": "2026-11-14T12:00:00Z",
    "lastLoginAt": null
  }
  ```

  ## Errors

  - 400: Email is already registered. or model validation.
  - 401: missing, invalid, or expired Bearer token.
  - 403: authenticated token with an insufficient role.

  Automatic model validation can return ValidationProblemDetails; explicit controller errors use a message field. Authentication middleware errors may have no body.

  ## Notes

  The response includes a Location header targeting the list action, not a user-detail endpoint. Captures userId on success. Use a unique newEmail; configure secret newPassword.

  Examples contain fictitious data. The assertion checks the successful scenario; a missing record or insufficient permissions can produce a different documented status.
}
